{"fingerprint":"025d2eb8ad06eef52f48ab03cb75a3fe802c9c251a19370998419240768b4d76","path":"src/review_gauntlet/cli.py","rule_id":"cli-contract","content":"`review` reports success even when some selected cells never produce a result. `review_cells_concurrently` can return without entries for futures that are cancelled during executor shutdown or fail to be tracked in an unexpected path, and `_cmd_review` indexes `results[selected.id]` directly. That raises an uncaught `KeyError`, bypassing the CLI's structured failure response and exit handling. Treat missing results as adapter failures so the CLI contract remains stable.","suggestion_code":"    for selected in selected_cells:
        outcome = results.get(selected.id)
        if outcome is None:
            outcome = ReviewAdapterError(
                f"review cell produced no result: {selected.id}",
                failure={"error": "missing review result", "cell_id": selected.id},
            )","existing_code":"    for selected in selected_cells:
        outcome = results[selected.id]","start_line":653,"end_line":654,"thinking":"CLI review commands should convert adapter execution anomalies into the documented failure payload rather than leaking KeyError.","imprecise":false}

